  <h2>AI-generated output</h2>
  <p>
    AI search, the AI assistants you connect to CAD Automation, and the learning paths written by AI can be wrong, incomplete, out of date or confidently mistaken. BIZOMAT designs these features so the AI chooses only among real pages and real tools, and so its CAD requests are checked before SOLIDWORKS acts on them, but no check catches every error. Treat AI output as a draft to review, not as a decision.
  </p>

  <h2>CAD automation and design validation</h2>
  <p>
    CAD Automation makes real changes to real SOLIDWORKS files on your computer. You are responsible for every model, assembly and drawing it produces or changes: check dimensions, tolerances, features, mates, materials, mass properties, drawing views, notes and title blocks against your requirements and the applicable standards before you use, release or manufacture from them. Keep backups and use your normal version control and release process. Automated checks, such as the kernel prediction of volume and size, reduce errors; they do not prove a design is fit for purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Engineering verification remains yours</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing produced with BIZOMAT, whether by a calculator, an AI assistant, CAD Automation or a Library chapter, replaces verification by a competent engineer. Not all work includes professional engineering certification, statutory approval, design sign-off or compliance certification, and BIZOMAT does not provide them unless that is expressly agreed in writing for a particular assignment and BIZOMAT is appropriately qualified and authorised to provide it. Work that legally requires a registered professional engineer, a licensed trade, a building certifier or another accredited professional must be carried out or reviewed by that professional.
  </p>

  <h2>Calculations and Resources</h2>
  <p>
    Tools, calculators, books, guides and examples are general information. Results depend on the inputs, units, assumptions and methods used, which may not suit your situation, and some methods simplify the physics. Check inputs, units and results, and confirm critical values against the relevant standards, codes and manufacturer data before relying on them.
  </p>

